{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Terms of Service | S2S{% endblock %}
{% block meta_description %}Terms governing beta access, accounts, subscriptions, menu content, and use of the S2S AI Menu Scanner.{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <section class="legal-hero">
        <div class="shell legal-hero-inner">
            <div><span class="eyebrow">Legal</span><h1>Terms of service</h1></div>
            <p>Last updated: 29 July 2026</p>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="legal-page">
        <div class="shell legal-layout">
            <aside class="legal-aside">
                <span class="material-symbols-outlined">gavel</span>
                <strong>Testing-stage terms</strong>
                <p>These terms document the current beta behavior and require legal review before commercial production use.</p>
            </aside>
            <article class="legal-content">
                <section><h2>1. Acceptance</h2><p>By creating an account or using S2S, you agree to these terms and the privacy policy. If you use the service for a business, you confirm that you are authorized to act for that business.</p></section>
                <section><h2>2. Beta service</h2><p>S2S and the AI Menu Scanner are under active development. Features may change, contain errors, or be temporarily unavailable. Beta output must not be treated as guaranteed accurate.</p></section>
                <section><h2>3. Accounts and security</h2><p>Each account must use one valid, unique email address. Email ownership must be verified before owner features become available. You are responsible for accurate registration information, protecting authentication credentials, maintaining access to your email, and activity performed through your account. Notify the project administrator if account access may be compromised.</p></section>
                <section><h2>4. Your content</h2><p>You retain responsibility for business information, menu images, item details, prices, translations, and other content submitted to S2S. You confirm that you have the right to upload and display it and that it does not violate law or third-party rights.</p></section>
                <section><h2>5. AI-assisted results and training records</h2><p>The scanner proposes text and structure from an image. You must review names, prices, allergens, descriptions, and all other results before saving or publishing. S2S is not responsible for losses caused by publishing incorrect information to the extent permitted by applicable law.</p><p>By separately accepting the AI Scanner data terms and submitting a scan, you authorize processing described in the Privacy Policy. Reviewed and corrected scan records may be retained after account deletion in de-linked or pseudonymized form for model evaluation and training. Do not submit images unless you have the right to provide their content for this purpose.</p></section>
                <section><h2>6. Acceptable use</h2><ul><li>Do not probe, disrupt, overload, or bypass service security.</li><li>Do not upload malicious, unlawful, infringing, or deceptive content.</li><li>Do not attempt unauthorized access to another account, menu, scan, or business.</li><li>Do not use the beta for safety-critical decisions.</li></ul></section>
                <section><h2>7. Trial and subscriptions</h2><p>After email verification, an unpaid owner receives one five-day trial with one business, one draft menu, one published menu, and three AI scan uses in total. No payment is required to begin the trial. When it ends, the dashboard, editor, owner menus, public menus, and scanner are paused until a paid plan becomes active. The owner can still choose a plan, return to the public home page, sign out, or permanently delete the account.</p><p>Paid plans are billed through Stripe according to the period selected at checkout. Plan limits apply to businesses and menu states. Changing or ending a subscription can pause public access, but does not by itself delete menu data. Prices and taxes shown at checkout control the actual charge.</p></section>
                <section><h2>8. Account deletion and termination</h2><p>You may cancel an active subscription or permanently delete the account through Account settings. Permanent deletion cannot be undone. Direct account and menu data is removed as described in the Privacy Policy; reviewed AI training records may remain in de-linked or pseudonymized form. The deleted email is represented by a keyed hash and blocked from new registration for 30 days to prevent repeated trial use.</p><p>We may restrict access when necessary to protect users, enforce these terms, perform maintenance, or respond to legal requirements.</p></section>
                <section><h2>9. Disclaimers</h2><p>The beta is provided on an "as available" basis without guarantees of uninterrupted availability, recognition accuracy, or suitability for a particular business purpose, to the extent permitted by law.</p></section>
                <section><h2>10. Changes</h2><p>These terms may change as S2S approaches production. Continued use after an updated version is published means you accept the revised terms.</p></section>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>
{% endblock %}
